eton. The coordinate-permuted derivative is continuous compactly supported on ℝⁿ, thus product-integrable by M001 before M003 is used. Euclidean coordinate permutation preserves Lebesgue measure: it permutes the orthonormal coordinate basis and preserves the volumes of boxes, which generate Borel Lebesgue measure. The factor Lebesgue measures are σ-finite, hence S-finite, and ℝ is real normed; therefore M003 applies and identifies the whole-space integral with the iterated integral, which is zero by the one-dimensional calculation. It follows that ∫∂_j g_j=0 and ∫(∂_j u_t)·u_{x_j}=−∫u_t·u_{x_jx_j}. Every such whole-space field is integrable by M001. Differentiate the exact Frobenius energy definition: e_t=2u_t·u_{tt}+2Σ_j u_{x_j}·∂_j u_t. Finite sums commute with integration. Summing the integration-by-parts identities and using Δ_xu=Σ_j u_{x_jx_j} gives E'(r)=2∫u_t·(u_{tt}−Δ_xu). Differentiating H001 gives 2u·u_t=0, hence u·u_t=0. At the same point H002 supplies a scalar a with u_{tt}−Δ_xu=a u. Taking the inner product with u_t gives u_t·(u_{tt}−Δ_xu)=a(u_t·u)=0. The zero integrand is integrable; thus E'(r)=0. No regularity of a is used, and arbitrary r>0 was fixed.\\\"}]}\"}","status":"completed"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"search_mathlib","description":"在固定 mathlib 的 Lean 源码中搜索正则表达式，返回至多 100 行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_mathlib","description":"读取固定 mathlib 中一个 Mathlib/...lean 文件的指定行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start_line":{"type":"integer"},"line_count":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start_line","line_count"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_task_input","description":"Read an explicitly frozen task document by ID; no other local files 